        <h2>1. About this document</h2>

        <p>
          You will see phrases like "applicable law" in this document. Many service providers ask you to agree to lengthy terms full of dense legal language, some of which may not be enforceable if challenged in court. Our approach is different: we write in plain English, use standard legal phrasing only where the law requires it, and do not try to override rights that applicable law gives you regardless of what we write.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you want to understand what "applicable law" means for your rights, see <a href="https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk/consumer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Citizens Advice</a>, <a href="https://www.gov.uk/unfair-terms-in-sales-contracts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOV.UK</a>, and <a href="https://www.which.co.uk/consumer-rights/regulations" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Which.co.uk</a>.
